pen board means nothing has been checked yet, not that everything is clean.
     <b>CLV</b> is the de-vigged close minus the de-vigged entry, in probability points, and it needs both sides
     of both prices; a leg missing any of them reads “no close”, never zero.
     <br><br>
     <b>The four lever columns are standings, not a forecast.</b> Only legs that <b>lost</b> are eligible, and on an
     open board nothing has lost yet — placing first on a lever means only this: if your leg loses and the draw
     reaches that lever, it stops on you. The highlighted placement in each column is where that lever stops right
     now. <b>Shortest odds</b> places the biggest favorite first and prints the submitted price, which is the
     same number it ranks on — a shorter price is a bigger favorite, always, so the column and its order can
     never come apart. <b>Last in</b> is numbered in the order the legs were filed, so the highlight sits at the
     <em>bottom</em> of that column — it is the only lever you can move by acting, and editing a leg refiles it.
     <b>Worst beat</b> and <b>Worst CLV</b> keep their columns while they wait: beat needs a final score, CLV needs
     a close with both sides at both ends. Both stay in the draw and pass while they cannot measure, which is
     dormant, not absent.`;
}

/* ---------------- where the levers stand, per leg ----------------
   The cascade is the one thing that decides who wears it, and the table used to show
   only its OUTPUT — a simulated percentage. Two of the four levers are readable straight
   off an open board: Shortest Odds is in the prices, Last In is in the timestamps. Those
   get a placement each. The other two cannot be computed before the games run and keep
   their column anyway, saying what they are waiting for — a lever nobody can see until
   it bites is the thing these columns exist to fix.

   ⚠️ STANDINGS OVER THE WHOLE POOL, NOT A PREDICTION. The cascade only ever looks at
   legs that LOST, and on an open board nothing has lost. Placing 1st is not "you are the
   bozo", it is "if your leg loses and the draw reaches this lever, it stops on you". The
   note under the table says so, because a column of placements with your name at the top
   reads as a verdict unless it is told not to.

   ⚠️ THE COLUMN PRINTS THE PRICE IT RANKS ON. simulate() and decide() both rank Shortest
   Odds on imp(), and imp() is monotonic in the American price — shorter price, higher
   implied, every time — so the submitted price and the placement are the same ordering
   and cannot come apart. That is the whole reason to print it. A de-vigged probability
   was shown here first: it is the better read of one leg in isolation, but it is NOT
   what the lever ranks on, so it could place a row below another that printed a smaller
   number, and it went blank on any leg filed without an opposite price. Both of those
   were the display disagreeing with the thing being displayed. The de-vig still does the
   work it is actually right for, one column over, where CLV needs it. */

// Competition ranking, descending on key: equal values share a placement and the next
// one skips. Ties are real here — two legs at the same price genuinely tie the lever,
// which is why the cascade has more than one rung.
function rankRows(rows, key){
  const out = rows.slice().sort((a,b)=>key(b)-key(a));
  let prev=null, r=0;
  out.forEach((row,i)=>{ const v=key(row); if(prev===null || v!==prev){ r=i+1; prev=v; } row.rank=r; });
  return out;
}

function leverStandings(live){
  const res = S.results || {};
  const d = live.map((x,i)=>{
    const r = res[kEnc(x.p)] || {};
    const pE = devigP(x.price, x.entryPriceOpp), pC = devigP(r.close, r.closeOpp);
    let beat = null;
    if(r.actual != null){
      const sd = sdOf(x);
      // A zero where zero is possible takes the floor rather than pretending a Bernoulli
      // outcome sits on the same scale as a point margin — same rule decide() applies.
      if(r.actual===0 && (x.mkt==='prop'||x.mkt==='total'||x.mkt==='other') && dirOf(x)==='over') beat = 999;
      else beat = beatDeficit(x.mkt, dirOf(x), x.mkt==='ml'?0:x.line,
                              x.mkt==='total'?null:r.actual, x.mkt==='total'?r.actual:null, sd);
    }
    // ⚠️ pE is the ENTRY de-vig, and it exists here only to make CLV — the Shortest odds
    // column ranks and prints the raw price. Do not route it back to that column.
    return { i, raw: imp(x.price), ts: x.ts||0, beat,
             clv: (pC==null||pE==null) ? null : (pC-pE) };
  });

  // rank[k][i] and holds[k][i], k being the lever index. Absent i = this lever cannot
  // rank that leg, which is a different statement from ranking it last.
  const rank = [{},{},{},{}], holds = [{},{},{},{}];
  const place = (k, rows, key, holder) => {
    if(!rows.length) return;
    rankRows(rows, key).forEach(r=>{ rank[k][r.i] = r.rank; });
    const h = holder(rows); if(h) holds[k][h.i] = true;
  };

  place(0, d.slice(), r=>r.raw, rows=>rows.reduce((a,b)=>b.raw>a.raw?b:a, rows[0]));
  const scored = d.filter(r=>r.beat!=null);
  place(1, scored, r=>r.beat, rows=>rows.reduce((a,b)=>b.beat>a.beat?b:a, rows[0]));
  // ⚠️ Last In is numbered in SUBMISSION order — 1st in, 2nd in — the same wording the
  // leg preview uses ("you'd be 3rd of 4 in"). The lever itself reads the OPPOSITE end
  // of that list, so the badge goes on the newest leg, not on 1st. Two orderings of one
  // column under one name is how a reader ends up sure of the wrong thing.
  place(2, d.slice(), r=>-r.ts, rows=>{ const h=rows.reduce((a,b)=>b.ts>a.ts?b:a, rows[0]); return h.ts>0?h:null; });
  const withClv = d.filter(r=>r.clv!=null);
  place(3, withClv, r=>-r.clv, rows=>rows.reduce((a,b)=>b.clv<a.clv?b:a, rows[0]));

  return { d, rank, holds, scored: scored.length, withClv: withClv.length };
}

/* Who is holding the belt right now.
   ⚠️ ONE definition, called by both the season board and the ticket. Two copies of this
   rule would eventually disagree about who is wearing it, on the same screen.

   ⚠️ It is the MOST RECENT bozo, not the season leader in bozos. `.fund` already means
   the second thing. Before this week is graded the holder is last week's — you keep it
   until somebody takes it off you, which is the entire idea of a belt. */
function beltHolder(){
  const now = S.bozo && playerName(S.bozo);
  if(now) return now;
  const hist = (S.history||[]).filter(h=>h&&h.bozo);
  return hist.length ? playerName(hist[hist.length-1].bozo) : null;
}

/* ---------------- season, as a split-flap board ---------------- */
// Dark plate in both themes, same call as .machine and .verdict. A chalkboard was
// considered: green field and handwriting fight the mono/terminal identity every
// other surface on this page uses, and it has no natural way to show a count change.
let lbPrev = {};
function paintTicker(players, t, mx, holder){
  const el=document.getElementById('lb');
  const rows = players.slice().sort((a,b)=>t[b]-t[a]||a.localeCompare(b));
  el.innerHTML =
    '<div class="thead"><span>#</span><span>Dawg</span><span>Bozos</span></div>' +
    rows.map((p,i)=>{
      const n=String(t[p]||0);
      const flaps=n.split('').map(ch=>`<b class="${t[p]?'':'zero'}">${ch}</b>`).join('');
      // data-worn drives the red nose next to the name — presence only, never a
      // count. The flap digits are the count; two encodings of one number can
      // disagree, and the nose is the one that would be wrong.
      // ⚠️ The belt supersedes the nose on the holder's row rather than sitting beside
      // it: holding it already implies having worn one, and two badges saying
      // overlapping things is how a row stops being readable at a glance.
      /* ⚠️ THE PLAQUE FOLLOWS THE BELT. "Funds this week" used to be computed from the
         season's highest bozo count, which is a different person the moment someone else
         is named — the demo showed Squatch holding the plaque while Tucholski held the
         belt, off the same board. In this game the bozo funds the NEXT ticket, so the
         plaque was describing the belt all along and measuring something else. One
         person, one rule, and `mx` is now only the sort order. */
      const holds = holder && p===holder;
      return `<div class="trow${ME&&p===ME.name?' me2':''}" data-worn="${t[p]?1:0}" data-belt="${holds?1:0}">
        <span class="rk">${i+1}</span>
        <span class="nm2">${esc(teamOf(p))}${holds?'<span class="fund">funds this week</span><span class="beltcrest" role="img" aria-label="Wearing the belt"></span>':''}</span>
        <span class="flap">${flaps}</span></div>`;
    }).join('');
  const trs=el.querySelectorAll('.trow');
  rows.forEach((p,i)=>{
    if(lbPrev[p]!==undefined && lbPrev[p]!==t[p] && trs[i])
      trs[i].querySelectorAll('.flap b').forEach(b=>b.classList.add('flip'));
    lbPrev[p]=t[p];
  });
  const total=Object.values(t).reduce((a,b)=>a+b,0);
  document.getElementById('lbMeta').textContent =
    total ? total+' ticket'+(total===1?'':'s')+' worn this season' : 'nobody has worn one yet';
}

/* ---------------- Toto's Bozo surface ----------------
   nav.js holds the surface-agnostic core prompt and the site manual. This is the block
   that tells Toto where he is and hands him the live numbers. It is regenerated on every
   question, so it can never go stale mid-conversation.

   ⚠️ The rule that matters here: Toto must not launder model output as observation. Bozo
   odds come out of a 20k-run simulation with known-soft inputs, so the caveats travel
   WITH the numbers rather than sitting in a footnote he can ignore. */
const BOZO_SYS = `RIGHT NOW you are on Bozo, a weekly group betting game inside the Data Dawgs site.
THE GAME: each member submits ONE leg. Every leg goes on ONE real parlay at DraftKings, funded by last week's bozo. Whoever busts it worst wears it and funds the next ticket.
- LEAGUE VISIBILITY: Bozo Boyz is listed for everyone; there is no longer a public Royale demo.
  Bozo Royale is still a live format any league can be created in — the demo league that showcased it was deleted. A signed-in person additionally sees only leagues they belong to or manage. The league picker beside the four page tabs uses that same filtered list.
- LEAGUE MEMBERSHIP: accounts authenticate people. A manager sets one shared league password under League Settings; after signing in, a person uses Join Existing League on the Bozo hub (or the duplicate control under Your Dawgs), chooses from up to 20 league names, and enters the password to add their own authenticated account. Never ask for or repeat the password. Per-person league invites, manager pre-adds and reusable join links are retired.
- Favorites only, inside the league's price band. No exact duplicate legs. The ticket LOCKS the moment the last leg lands; that moment is the close.
- Only legs that LOST are eligible to be the bozo. Nobody who cashed can wear it, no matter how bad the price was.
- Each week the tiebreaker hierarchy is a FRESH RANDOM PERMUTATION of the league's live levers, drawn on the server and written once. It is not a weighted score and not a fixed cascade. Walk the drawn order; the first lever that isolates one person names the bozo; ties fall to the next lever down.
- The four levers: Shortest Odds (biggest favorite in the pool), Worst Beat (finished furthest under its number, measured in standard deviations), Last In (final leg submitted), Worst CLV (price moved most against it).
- The randomisation is the design, not decoration: it keeps each lever legible while making the meta unsolvable. Do not suggest replacing it with a composite score — that was considered and rejected, because any weighted blend is just a new deterministic objective someone will solve.
HOW TO TALK ABOUT THE NUMBERS:
- "Bozo odds" and "leg wins" are SIMULATION output, not observation. Say so whenever you quote them.
- The simulation draws every leg INDEPENDENTLY. Two legs on the same game are not independent. If the state flags correlated legs, mention it rather than quoting the cash probability as if it were clean.
- Prop legs use a placeholder standard deviation (line x 0.55) that is openly a guess. Flag a prop before leaning on its Worst Beat exposure.
- Worst CLV is measured only when both sides of the DraftKings entry and both sides of the kickoff close were captured. A missing side is unmeasured, never zero, and the lever passes it.
- priceSource=captured means the Worker fetched both DraftKings sides through SGO at submit and froze them for confirmation. priceSource=self is limited to unresolved props and Other legs; those are visibly badged and clvEligible=false. Never mix self-priced legs into CLV.
- The "As it stands / If every leg lost" panel is a read-only hypothetical over currently filed legs. It assumes every filed leg loses, does not know results, and never names a bozo. Before the card locks there is no running order at all. Never present the panel as a prediction, a probability, or a graded outcome.
- You may NOT place, edit or remove anyone's leg, and you must never tell someone their bet is guaranteed. Prices and probabilities, never certainties.`;

function bozoCtx(){
  if(onHub()) return 'The user is on the Bozo league directory, not inside a league. '
    + (LEAGUES.length ? 'Leagues: ' + LEAGUES.map(l=>`${l.name} (${l.size} members, week ${l.week||1}, ${l.status||'open'})`).join('; ')
                      : 'No leagues are loaded.');
  const players = names();
  if(!players.length) return 'No league is loaded on this device yet.';
  const picks = S.picks||{}, res = S.results||{}, status = S.status||'open';
  const st = settings(), bd = band(), lg = league();
  const live = players.map(p=>({p, ...(picks[kEnc(p)]||{})})).filter(x=>x.price!=null);
  const levers = (st.levers && st.levers.length) ? st.levers : [0,1,2,3];
  const L=[];

  L.push(`LEAGUE: ${lg?lg.name:LID} — ${players.length} members, season ${S.season||2026}, week ${S.week||1}, status ${status}.`);
  L.push(`WHO IS ASKING: ${ME ? teamOf(ME.name)+(isManager()?' (league manager)':'') : 'not signed in — they can read the board but cannot submit'}.`);
  L.push(`RULES IN FORCE: price band ${bd.ceil} to ${bd.floor}; stake $${st.stake??50} on the ticket; duplicate selections and contradicting sides are ALWAYS refused (the ticket is one real DraftKings parlay); editing a leg ${st.allowEdit?'stays open until the ticket is placed (and resets your timestamp AND your price)':'is locked once your leg is in'}; the ticket places ${st.lockRule==='count'?`at ${st.lockCount} legs`:'when every member is in'}.`);
  L.push(`LEVERS IN THE DRAW (${levers.length} of 4): ${levers.map(i=>LEVERS[i].name).join(', ')}.`);

  L.push(`THE TICKET (${live.length} of ${players.length} in, listed in submission order — the LAST one is currently exposed to Last In):`);
  live.slice().sort((a,b)=>(a.ts||0)-(b.ts||0)).forEach((x,i)=>{
    const r=res[kEnc(x.p)]||{};
    const outcome = status==='graded' ? (r.won===true?' WON':r.won===false?' LOST':' push/void') : '';
    L.push(`${i+1}. ${teamOf(x.p)} | ${x.label} | ${x.price} | ${SPORTS[x.sport]?SPORTS[x.sport].n:x.sport} ${x.game}${(x.mkt==='prop'||x.mkt==='other')?` (${x.mkt.toUpperCase()} — soft SD, manual grading)`:''} | in ${when(x.ts)}${outcome}${r.actual!=null?` | finished ${r.actual}`:''}`);
  });
  const missing = players.filter(p=>picks[kEnc(p)]==null);
  if(missing.length) L.push(`NOT IN YET: ${missing.map(teamOf).join(', ')}. The ticket cannot place until they are${st.lockRule==='count'?' (unless the leg count trips first)':''}.`);

  if(live.length){
    const offDec = live.reduce((a,x)=>a*dec(x.price),1);
    const fairDec = 1/live.reduce((a,x)=>a*devig(x.price),1);
    L.push(`PARLAY: offered ${amer(offDec)}, de-vigged fair ${amer(fairDec)}, so the book keeps ${pct(1-offDec/fairDec)} across the legs. $${st.stake??50} returns $${Math.round(offDec*(st.stake??50)).toLocaleString()} if it cashes.`);
    // Only quote the sim if the CACHED run matches the board as it stands right now.
    if(simOut && simKey === simKeyFor(live, levers, status)){
      L.push(`SIMULATION (${simOut.sims.toLocaleString()} runs, legs drawn independently — MODEL OUTPUT, NOT OBSERVED):`);
      L.push(`- ticket cashes ${pct(simOut.cash)}`);
      live.forEach((x,i)=>L.push(`- ${teamOf(x.p)}: leg wins ${pct(simOut.win[i])}, bozo odds ${pct(simOut.bozo[i])}, only-loser ${pct(simOut.solo[i])}${simOut.by[i]?`, usually named by ${simOut.by[i].name}`:''}`));
    } else {
      L.push(`SIMULATION: not currently computed for this board. Do not quote bozo odds — say they are on the board's diagnostics panel.`);
    }
    const byEv={}; live.forEach(x=>{ const k=x.eventId||x.game; if(k)(byEv[k]=byEv[k]||[]).push(x); });
    const stacked=Object.values(byEv).filter(g=>g.length>1);
    if(stacked.length) L.push(`⚠️ CORRELATED LEGS — independence is violated: ` +
      stacked.map(g=>`${g[0].game} (${g.map(x=>teamOf(x.p)).join(', ')})`).join('; ') + '. The cash number above is wrong in an unknown direction.');
  }

  const ord=S.order;
  L.push(ord && ord.length
    ? `HIERARCHY DRAWN for this week: ${ord.map((li,i)=>`${i+1}. ${LEVERS[li].name}`).join(', ')}.`
    : `HIERARCHY NOT DRAWN YET — the order is decided on the server when the last leg lands. Do not guess it.`);
  if(S.bozo) L.push(`THIS WEEK'S BOZO: ${teamOf(playerName(S.bozo))} — ${S.bozoWhy||''}`);
  const fl = flaggedRows();
  L.push(fl.length
    ? `FLAGGED FOR REVIEW (${fl.length}): submitted price far from the close. NOT an accusation — a real steam move can do this. Report it neutrally if asked and never call anyone a cheat:\n`
      + fl.slice(0,8).map(x=>`- ${teamOf(x.r.player)} w${x.r.week} ${x.r.label}: ${x.f.why}`).join('\n')
    : `FLAGGED FOR REVIEW: none. ⚠️ Note that closing prices are not captured yet, so this check is DORMANT rather than passing — say "nothing is being checked yet", not "everything looks clean".`);

  const t={}; players.forEach(p=>t[p]=0);
  (S.history||[]).forEach(h=>{ const b=h&&h.bozo&&playerName(h.bozo); if(b&&t[b]!=null) t[b]++; });
  const bzNow=S.bozo&&playerName(S.bozo); if(bzNow&&t[bzNow]!=null) t[bzNow]++;
  const mx=Math.max(0,...Object.values(t));
  L.push(`SEASON (bozos worn): ` + players.slice().sort((a,b)=>t[b]-t[a]||a.localeCompare(b))
    .map(p=>`${teamOf(p)} ${t[p]}${t[p]===mx&&mx>0?' (funds this week)':''}`).join(', '));

  if(ME){
    const rows=sheetRows(ME.name);
    if(rows.length){
      const w=rows.filter(r=>resOf(r)==='won').length, l=rows.filter(r=>resOf(r)==='lost').length;
      L.push(`THE ASKER'S RECORD: ${w}-${l} across ${rows.length} logged legs. Recent: `
        + rows.slice(0,5).map(r=>`w${r.week} ${r.label} ${r.price} ${resOf(r)||'open'}`).join('; '));
    } else L.push(`THE ASKER'S RECORD: nothing in the ledger yet — it starts writing when a week locks.`);
  }
  return L.join('\n');
}
